      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 10.02,
      "font_name": "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu",
      "is_math": false,
      "char_count": 335,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.25036_p16_b21",
      "text": "As shown in the table, LBP consistently outperforms both the standard DPO and the Modified DPO (DPOM) baselines\non this larger scale. Specifically, LBP maintains a clear advantage on hallucination-centric benchmarks (MMHalBench,\nAMBER Generative Task, and Object HalBench) as the dataset size increases, while achieving comparable performance on\nthe Discriminative Task. These results confirm that our method scales effectively with data size, robustly maintaining its\nadvantage over competitive baselines.\n",
      "bbox": [
